          "path": "_m/g/f/q/0/macduff-aberdeenshire-wp/institution-street-geograph-or.jpg",
          "filename": "Institution Street - geograph.org.uk - 861451.jpg",
          "caption": "Institution Street Looking up from the harbour. I think the crowstepped and turreted building must be a private house. The red triangle outside the council offices one block up the street probably contains a leading light to guide vessels safely into the harbour at night. These are normally in pairs, sited so that when one is seen directly above the other, the vessel is on the correct course, but in this case I could not see a second one.",
